Problem 4: Leaky capacitor

A parallel-plate capacitor of capacitance $C_0$ is filled with a weakly conducting layered medium with $\varepsilon = 1$, whose resistivity depends on the distance $x$ from one of the plates according to the law $\rho = \rho_0\left(1+\frac{2x}{d}\right)$, where $d$ is the distance between the plates of the capacitor. The capacitor is connected to a battery of voltage $U_0$ (Fig. 14).

https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Eisatopon/physics-olympiads-bank/main/images/russia-2011-1-4-fig1.png

Fig. 14

Find:

1. the current flowing through the capacitor;

2. the charges of the lower ($q_1$) and upper ($q_2$) plates of the capacitor;

3. the charge $q$ inside the capacitor (i.e. in the medium between the plates);

4. the electric energy $W_{\mathrm{e}}$ stored in the capacitor.

Problem 2: With a puff of smoke

During aerial photography a photograph was obtained on which two smoke plumes from steam locomotives are visible (Fig. 9.1). One cell of the photograph corresponds to $50\,\mathrm{m}$ on the ground. It is known that one locomotive moved uniformly along a circular railway line, and the other moved with the same speed along a straight line.

Determine:

• the direction of the wind velocity;
• the radius $R$ of the circular railway;
• the ratio of the speed $v$ of the locomotive to the wind speed $u$;
• the direction of the straight railway line (carry out the constructions with compasses and a ruler).

